<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.4.xsd">

    <!--
    CVE-2026-53514 (better-auth organization-invitation email-ownership bypass)

    NVD's CPE match for this CVE is versionStartIncluding=1.6.14 with NO
    upper bound, so every better-auth release from 1.6.14 onward is flagged
    forever, even though the upstream fix shipped well before our version:

      - PR #9577 (merged for the 1.6.11 release, then needed a follow-up
        because 1.6.14 reintroduced the gap for non-default configs):
        https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/pull/9577
      - PR #9877 "fix(organization): split invitation verification gates"
        (merged 2026-06-02, included in 1.7.0 and all later 1.7.x):
        https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth/pull/9877

    We are on better-auth 1.7.6, which contains both fixes, and our own
    config in packages/auth/auth.ts additionally sets
    `requireEmailVerificationOnInvitation: true` on the organization plugin
    as defense in depth. This is a stale/incomplete NVD record, not an
    unpatched dependency — remove this suppression once NVD adds a
    versionEndExcluding bound and dependency-check stops matching 1.7.x.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes><![CDATA[
        False positive: NVD CPE match has no upper version bound for
        CVE-2026-53514, so it matches every better-auth >=1.6.14 including
        our current 1.7.6, which already contains the fix (better-auth
        PR #9577 and PR #9877). See comment above for detail.
        ]]></notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:npm/better\-auth@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53514</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>
